From dbdf960a3362b719cafd726377085ee63dfdff35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Vit <martin@voipmonitor.org>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 05:38:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(mla): keep SM12x cuBLAS input batches disjoint

Use disjoint query and value projection matrices on SM120/121 to avoid the documented cuBLAS overlapping-stride read defect. Preserve head-major DCP reduce-scatter storage so value projection does not add a transpose copy. Tensor values, collective reduction and CUDA graph support are unchanged.

Validation: 26 mapped-allocation, changed-input graph, random GEMM and rank-layout cases passed on RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell. The unmodified four-token value GEMM reproduces a native MMU fault exactly at the mapped allocation end.

Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>

Signed-off-by: Martin Vit <martin@voipmonitor.org>
(cherry picked from commit 9aa73287b12ee76114105e6fb838003e62b6d030)
